Third-party colour palettes
===========================

The JSON files in this directory, except preman-dark.json, are vendored verbatim from openchamber
by way of preman (https://github.com/openchamber/openchamber, packages/ui/src/lib/theme/themes/):

    Copyright (c) 2025 Bohdan Triapitsyn
    MIT

preman-dark.json is preman's own dark theme (MIT), written out by hand in the same shape.

They are copied rather than depended on because they are data, not code, and TableCraft does not
ship them: `scripts/generate-themes.ts` reads them when run by hand, and the audited result is
what is committed under `src/appearance/themes/` (decision 064). This directory is in
`.prettierignore`, so re-vendoring is a readable diff instead of a reflow.

openchamber's files are themselves ports of upstream colour schemes. Each generated theme carries
the `source` and `licence` of its row below, and Settings shows them beside its name. Every scheme
is MIT except JetBrains, which is Apache-2.0.

